# HTTP server & routes

This product serves on Fiber v3 (`fib.HTTP(app.Addr)`) and collects every
`stack.Route`. Swapping to the net/http paved road is one line: `stack.HTTP(addr)`
— routes, auth, ops, and decoration keep working either way.

- Contribute a route by providing a `stack.Route` from any module (or, typed,
  via `api.Handle` — see `references/presets/api.md`).
- Every route declares policy: `Require: "perm"`, `Require: "policy:name"`, or
  `Public: true`. Zero value = any authenticated caller.
- `stack.OpsRoutes` adds `/healthz` (causal, 503 on degraded), `/ops/blast`,
  `/ops/graph`. `fib.Route`/`fib.Option` add fiber-native handlers/middleware;
  guard those with fiber middleware (`auth.Protect` covers stack.Routes only).

